    "breadcrumb": "AWS Workshop Report \u003e Workshop",
    "content": "Workshop Overview\r1. Why AWS CDK?\rTraditionally, Infrastructure as Code (IaC) relied on static YAML/JSON templates. AWS CDK allows developers to define cloud resources using familiar programming languages like TypeScript. This brings strong typing, autocompletion, inheritance, and code reuse to cloud infrastructure definition.\n2. Serverless Event-Driven Architecture\rModern web applications require high reliability and cost-efficiency. This workshop demonstrates a Serverless Event-Driven Architecture that scales automatically to handle traffic spikes and guarantees high availability without active server administration.\nWe will use Amazon API Gateway for REST endpoints, AWS Lambda for serverless compute, Amazon DynamoDB for scalable single-table data storage, Amazon SQS for message queuing, and Amazon EventBridge for custom event routing.",
