    "breadcrumb": "AWS Workshop Report",
    "content": "This section lists and introduces the blogs you have posted in the AWS Study Group.\nBlog 1 - Simplify AWS AppSync Events integration with Powertools for AWS Lambda\rThis blog introduces a new AppSyncEventsResolver feature in Powertools for AWS Lambda (supported in Python, TypeScript, and .NET), which simplifies integration with AWS AppSync Events for real-time applications such as chat apps, dashboards, or IoT systems.\nBlog 2 - Breaking AI Agent Stale Knowledge with Web Search on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore\rThis post introduces the newly General Availability (GA) Web Search capability on Amazon Bedrock AgentCore, a fully managed, MCP-compatible solution that enables AI Agents to bypass frozen training data by accessing real-time web search results.\nBlog 3 - Simplifying Multi-App Management in AWS Amplify Hosting with Unified Webhooks\rThis post covers how Unified Webhooks on AWS Amplify Hosting resolves git provider webhook limits for monorepos, allowing team developers to connect multiple Amplify applications to a single repository with a single unified webhook.",
